{"jobs":[{"id":"eaf53e57-0876-48a2-a583-3c042470f409","title":"Operations Specialist","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T20:06:34.567+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/eaf53e57-0876-48a2-a583-3c042470f409","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/eaf53e57-0876-48a2-a583-3c042470f409/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>Company Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Job Overview</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SimpleClosure is looking for an Operations Specialist to guide founders through the company dissolution process from start to finish. In this role, you'll serve as the main point of contact for clients navigating one of the most difficult moments in their business journey—translating complex legal, tax, and administrative requirements into a clear, manageable plan. You'll balance high-touch client support with process-oriented thinking, helping us continuously refine how we deliver shutdown services at scale. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a fast-paced startup environment, enjoys solving ambiguous problems, and finds fulfillment in helping people through challenging transitions with empathy and professionalism.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary point of contact for clients, introducing them to their personalized shutdown plans, guiding them through the dissolution process, and addressing their queries and concerns along the way.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capture, document, and optimize processes to enhance operational efficiency and client satisfaction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with internal teams to ensure smooth operations and timely resolution of client issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize Slack, Google Suite, Notion and other remote tools for efficient communication and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cultivate an understanding of our services, processes, and legal requirements related to shutting down.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide exceptional customer service, demonstrating empathy and professionalism with client interactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist clients in gathering necessary documentation and information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure accurate and timely updates to clients regarding their progress.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain organized and accurate records of all company dissolution activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with external parties such as government agencies, regulatory bodies, and legal counsel to ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively identify opportunities to improve our internal processes and workflows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Start-up experience preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to multitask and follow through on projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and spoken English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional problem-solving and interpersonal skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in operations, legal, or accounting a plus</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Salary: $65,000 to $75,000, depending on experience level and location</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote work environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nSimpleClosure is looking for an Operations Specialist to guide founders through the company dissolution process from start to finish. In this role, you'll serve as the main point of contact for clients navigating one of the most difficult moments in their business journey—translating complex legal, tax, and administrative requirements into a clear, manageable plan. You'll balance high-touch client support with process-oriented thinking, helping us continuously refine how we deliver shutdown services at scale. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a fast-paced startup environment, enjoys solving ambiguous problems, and finds fulfillment in helping people through challenging transitions with empathy and professionalism.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Serve as the primary point of contact for clients, introducing them to their personalized shutdown plans, guiding them through the dissolution process, and addressing their queries and concerns along the way.\n\n - Capture, document, and optimize processes to enhance operational efficiency and client satisfaction.\n\n - Collaborate closely with internal teams to ensure smooth operations and timely resolution of client issues.\n\n - Utilize Slack, Google Suite, Notion and other remote tools for efficient communication and documentation.\n\n - Cultivate an understanding of our services, processes, and legal requirements related to shutting down.\n\n - Provide exceptional customer service, demonstrating empathy and professionalism with client interactions.\n\n - Assist clients in gathering necessary documentation and information.\n\n - Ensure accurate and timely updates to clients regarding their progress.\n\n - Maintain organized and accurate records of all company dissolution activities.\n\n - Coordinate with external parties such as government agencies, regulatory bodies, and legal counsel to ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulations.\n\n - Proactively identify opportunities to improve our internal processes and workflows.\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Bachelor’s degree\n\n - Start-up experience preferred\n\n - Ability to multitask and follow through on projects\n\n - Excellent written and spoken English communication skills\n\n - Exceptional problem-solving and interpersonal skills\n\n - Experience in operations, legal, or accounting a plus\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Base Salary: $65,000 to $75,000, depending on experience level and location\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Remote work environment\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3ccc8e03-46c6-494a-97f9-2978623fee89","title":"Mid-Level Full Stack Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-20T16:52:39.278+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/3ccc8e03-46c6-494a-97f9-2978623fee89","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/3ccc8e03-46c6-494a-97f9-2978623fee89/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Company Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SimpleClosure is seeking a Mid-Level Full Stack Engineer to join our growing engineering team. In this role, you’ll work across the stack to build, improve, and scale core product functionality that directly impacts our customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work in a small pod with dedicated product and design support, shipping in short cycles alongside the internal teams who use the platform every day. This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys owning features end to end – balancing frontend craftsmanship with backend problem-solving in a fast-moving startup environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>*</strong>Candidates <u>MUST</u> be located in the New York City Metro area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain full-stack features across the SimpleClosure platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Product, Design additional stakeholders to translate requirements into scalable technical solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement clean, maintainable frontend experiences using Next.js, React and TypeScript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and integrate backend services, APIs, and data models to support product workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write high-quality, well-tested code and participate in code reviews</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own features end-to-end, from technical design through deployment and iteration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Debug, troubleshoot, and resolve issues in production environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously improve development processes, tooling, and code quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience: 3–5 years of professional software engineering experience, ideally in a startup or fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Frontend: Strong experience with React and TypeScript; Next.js or similar frameworks preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backend: Experience building server-side logic, APIs and integrating with third party services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Databases: Familiarity with relational and/or NoSQL databases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership: Comfortable taking projects from concept through deployment and iteration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Problem-Solving: Proactive, thoughtful engineer who can navigate ambiguity and make sound technical decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboration: Strong team player who enjoys working cross-functionally</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communication: Clear written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adaptability: Thrives in an evolving startup environment with shifting priorities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Salary: $120,000 - $170,000, depending on experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (currently 2 days per week in office)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nSimpleClosure is seeking a Mid-Level Full Stack Engineer to join our growing engineering team. In this role, you’ll work across the stack to build, improve, and scale core product functionality that directly impacts our customers.\n\nYou'll work in a small pod with dedicated product and design support, shipping in short cycles alongside the internal teams who use the platform every day. This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys owning features end to end – balancing frontend craftsmanship with backend problem-solving in a fast-moving startup environment.\n\n*Candidates MUST be located in the New York City Metro area.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Design, build, and maintain full-stack features across the SimpleClosure platform\n\n - Collaborate with Product, Design additional stakeholders to translate requirements into scalable technical solutions\n\n - Implement clean, maintainable frontend experiences using Next.js, React and TypeScript\n\n - Build and integrate backend services, APIs, and data models to support product workflows\n\n - Write high-quality, well-tested code and participate in code reviews\n\n - Own features end-to-end, from technical design through deployment and iteration\n\n - Debug, troubleshoot, and resolve issues in production environments\n\n - Continuously improve development processes, tooling, and code quality\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Experience: 3–5 years of professional software engineering experience, ideally in a startup or fast-paced environment\n\n - Frontend: Strong experience with React and TypeScript; Next.js or similar frameworks preferred\n\n - Backend: Experience building server-side logic, APIs and integrating with third party services\n\n - Databases: Familiarity with relational and/or NoSQL databases\n\n - Ownership: Comfortable taking projects from concept through deployment and iteration\n\n - Problem-Solving: Proactive, thoughtful engineer who can navigate ambiguity and make sound technical decisions\n\n - Collaboration: Strong team player who enjoys working cross-functionally\n\n - Communication: Clear written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Adaptability: Thrives in an evolving startup environment with shifting priorities\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Base Salary: $120,000 - $170,000, depending on experience level\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (currently 2 days per week in office)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9ed21363-c18f-4db4-afa0-61d6bf75b9aa","title":"Commercial Account Executive","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-24T21:38:12.616+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/9ed21363-c18f-4db4-afa0-61d6bf75b9aa","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/9ed21363-c18f-4db4-afa0-61d6bf75b9aa/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Company Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a driven and dynamic Commercial Account Executive to support our sales efforts, engage with potential clients, and help grow our customer base. The ideal candidate has a passion for sales, strong communication skills, and a desire to work in a fast-paced startup environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities </strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in identifying, researching, and qualifying prospective customers navigating business closures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the sales team in managing the sales pipeline and tracking key metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide product demonstrations and educate potential clients on our solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support deal progression by managing follow-ups, next steps, and customer questions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with marketing to optimize lead generation and conversion strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of sales activities in CRM software (e.g., HubSpot, Salesforce).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and report customer feedback to help refine sales strategies and product development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay up-to-date with industry trends, competitor activity, and client needs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal background, understanding of M&amp;A, corporate law, or accounting experience (preferred but not necessary)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2 - 4+ years sales experience in SaaS/Startup environment; in Legal-tech, Fintech, HR-tech.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills with a customer-first mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently, stay organized, and manage multiple priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable conducting outreach and engaging with potential clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM tools like HubSpot or Salesforce (preferred but not required).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enthusiastic, goal-oriented, and eager to learn in a startup environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing, or a related field.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation: OTE range for this role is $150,000–$180,000. Compensation is determined based on experience, qualifications, and geographic market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote work environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe are seeking a driven and dynamic Commercial Account Executive to support our sales efforts, engage with potential clients, and help grow our customer base. The ideal candidate has a passion for sales, strong communication skills, and a desire to work in a fast-paced startup environment.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES \n\n - Assist in identifying, researching, and qualifying prospective customers navigating business closures\n\n - Support the sales team in managing the sales pipeline and tracking key metrics.\n\n - Provide product demonstrations and educate potential clients on our solutions.\n\n - Support deal progression by managing follow-ups, next steps, and customer questions\n\n - Collaborate with marketing to optimize lead generation and conversion strategies.\n\n - Maintain accurate records of sales activities in CRM software (e.g., HubSpot, Salesforce).\n\n - Gather and report customer feedback to help refine sales strategies and product development.\n\n - Stay up-to-date with industry trends, competitor activity, and client needs.\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Legal background, understanding of M&A, corporate law, or accounting experience (preferred but not necessary)\n\n - 2 - 4+ years sales experience in SaaS/Startup environment; in Legal-tech, Fintech, HR-tech.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills with a customer-first mindset.\n\n - Ability to work independently, stay organized, and manage multiple priorities.\n\n - Comfortable conducting outreach and engaging with potential clients.\n\n - Experience with CRM tools like HubSpot or Salesforce (preferred but not required).\n\n - Enthusiastic, goal-oriented, and eager to learn in a startup environment.\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing, or a related field.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Compensation: OTE range for this role is $150,000–$180,000. Compensation is determined based on experience, qualifications, and geographic market.\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Remote work environment\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8f2a5d2c-340c-4a18-bb30-d1294171c899","title":"Strategy & Operations - Asset Hub","department":"Asset Hub","team":"Asset Hub","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-05T23:06:37.089+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/8f2a5d2c-340c-4a18-bb30-d1294171c899","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/8f2a5d2c-340c-4a18-bb30-d1294171c899/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About the Company</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we're headed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company's life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a dynamic and results-driven Strategy &amp; Operations to join our AssetHub team. AssetHub helps our customers sell proprietary assets to buyers; returning value to founders, investors, and lenders through unique partnerships with leading AI companies and other buyers. We're experiencing fast growth and have the potential to build a massive new marketplace, making this a unique opportunity to join early and shape a product with real impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own the full operational lifecycle of our supply side (asset sellers), from initial outreach through deal close. You'll track where customers are in their journey, ensure nothing falls through the cracks, and build and optimize the systems that make it all run and scale. We use AI extensively (including Claude) to automate where possible, and we want someone who leans into that, not away from it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is both internal and external facing. We're looking for someone that puts customers first and is feels warm inside when their holistic experience with us is amazing. It is not a typical CSM role, however - our customers are founders of small and medium-sized businesses, and our engagement with them is short. Success here is about earning trust quickly, guiding founders through an unfamiliar process with clarity and empathy, and maximizing the value returned to everyone involved, with as little friction for the founder as possible.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>*</strong>Candidates <u>MUST</u> be located in the New York City Metro area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities </strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Maximize asset supply</strong> — Proactively work to maximize the number of high-quality assets listed in our catalog. This means constantly evaluating and optimizing our customer funnel with product and ops teams, to convert the most leads into active asset sellers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the customer lifecycle end-to-end</strong> — Track and manage customer progress from first contact through deal execution. Identify when customers are stuck and unblock them with minimal effort required on their end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Guide founders through the process</strong> — Be the empathetic, knowledgeable point of contact for founders considering or actively completing an asset sale. Understand their concerns, answer their questions, and communicate clearly throughout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build and automate workflows</strong> — Identify repetitive or manual steps in the process and build systems (with AI tools like Claude and platforms like HubSpot) to automate them, improving both throughput and customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive cross-functional initiatives</strong> — Collaborate with marketing, sales, engineering, and product to build scalable growth loops and improve the seller experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Launch and grow new offerings</strong> — Act as both thought partner and operator, with the autonomy to conceptualize and build new services within AssetHub.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in sales/CS/operations in SaaS/Startup environment (or an MBA and 3+ years of the same experience)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are commercially minded. You understand what moves a deal forward. You know how to build trust with founders and you know how to close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are results oriented and enjoy seeing a customer happy with your service.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are independent and proactive, and also comfortable being scrappy and adapting as we move fast.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a track record of driving projects across teams and stakeholders — including product, engineering, legal, finance and marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are operationally minded, detail-oriented but strategic enough to see how your work connects to bigger goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a self starter - you don't wait to be told what to fix. You identify the gap, propose the solution, and move.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some technical familiarity and comfort with CRM platforms and data management tools are a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills with a customer-first mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently, stay organized, initiate processes and manage multiple priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable engaging with potential clients, closing deals, and executing on them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enthusiastic, goal-oriented, and eager to learn in a startup environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM tools like HubSpot or Salesforce and workflow/data tools (preferred but not required).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working within Legal-tech, Fintech, HR-tech (preferred but not required).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing, or a related field.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation: Total package of $110,000 - $165,000 (this includes base pay and variable compensation) - based on experience and location </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OTE is 80/20 base/variable split</p></li></ul></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employer Covered Medical Benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hybrid work in NYC (two days in office, three days remote)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two in-person team retreats a year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) retirement plan with Traditional &amp; Roth options and immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT THE COMPANY\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.\n\nAs the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we're headed.\n\nJoining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company's life.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe're looking for a dynamic and results-driven Strategy & Operations to join our AssetHub team. AssetHub helps our customers sell proprietary assets to buyers; returning value to founders, investors, and lenders through unique partnerships with leading AI companies and other buyers. We're experiencing fast growth and have the potential to build a massive new marketplace, making this a unique opportunity to join early and shape a product with real impact.\n\nYou'll own the full operational lifecycle of our supply side (asset sellers), from initial outreach through deal close. You'll track where customers are in their journey, ensure nothing falls through the cracks, and build and optimize the systems that make it all run and scale. We use AI extensively (including Claude) to automate where possible, and we want someone who leans into that, not away from it.\n\nThis role is both internal and external facing. We're looking for someone that puts customers first and is feels warm inside when their holistic experience with us is amazing. It is not a typical CSM role, however - our customers are founders of small and medium-sized businesses, and our engagement with them is short. Success here is about earning trust quickly, guiding founders through an unfamiliar process with clarity and empathy, and maximizing the value returned to everyone involved, with as little friction for the founder as possible.\n\n*Candidates MUST be located in the New York City Metro area.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES \n\n - Maximize asset supply — Proactively work to maximize the number of high-quality assets listed in our catalog. This means constantly evaluating and optimizing our customer funnel with product and ops teams, to convert the most leads into active asset sellers.\n\n - Own the customer lifecycle end-to-end — Track and manage customer progress from first contact through deal execution. Identify when customers are stuck and unblock them with minimal effort required on their end.\n\n - Guide founders through the process — Be the empathetic, knowledgeable point of contact for founders considering or actively completing an asset sale. Understand their concerns, answer their questions, and communicate clearly throughout.\n\n - Build and automate workflows — Identify repetitive or manual steps in the process and build systems (with AI tools like Claude and platforms like HubSpot) to automate them, improving both throughput and customer experience.\n\n - Drive cross-functional initiatives — Collaborate with marketing, sales, engineering, and product to build scalable growth loops and improve the seller experience.\n\n - Launch and grow new offerings — Act as both thought partner and operator, with the autonomy to conceptualize and build new services within AssetHub.\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 5+ years of experience in sales/CS/operations in SaaS/Startup environment (or an MBA and 3+ years of the same experience)\n\n - You are commercially minded. You understand what moves a deal forward. You know how to build trust with founders and you know how to close.\n\n - You are results oriented and enjoy seeing a customer happy with your service.\n\n - You are independent and proactive, and also comfortable being scrappy and adapting as we move fast.\n\n - You have a track record of driving projects across teams and stakeholders — including product, engineering, legal, finance and marketing.\n\n - You are operationally minded, detail-oriented but strategic enough to see how your work connects to bigger goals.\n\n - You are a self starter - you don't wait to be told what to fix. You identify the gap, propose the solution, and move.\n\n - Some technical familiarity and comfort with CRM platforms and data management tools are a plus.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills with a customer-first mindset.\n\n - Ability to work independently, stay organized, initiate processes and manage multiple priorities.\n\n - Comfortable engaging with potential clients, closing deals, and executing on them.\n\n - Enthusiastic, goal-oriented, and eager to learn in a startup environment.\n\n - Experience with CRM tools like HubSpot or Salesforce and workflow/data tools (preferred but not required).\n\n - Experience working within Legal-tech, Fintech, HR-tech (preferred but not required).\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing, or a related field.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Compensation: Total package of $110,000 - $165,000 (this includes base pay and variable compensation) - based on experience and location \n   \n   - OTE is 80/20 base/variable split\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Employer Covered Medical Benefits\n\n - Unlimited PTO\n\n - Hybrid work in NYC (two days in office, three days remote)\n\n - Two in-person team retreats a year\n\n - 401(k) retirement plan with Traditional & Roth options and immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a2f4ca92-8baf-401b-80b2-8db05c8897b6","title":"VC/Accelerator Partnerships","department":"Partnerships","team":"Partnerships","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote in San Francisco","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-12T19:07:40.931+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/a2f4ca92-8baf-401b-80b2-8db05c8897b6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/a2f4ca92-8baf-401b-80b2-8db05c8897b6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About the Company</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This isn't a sales role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It's a relationships role — built on genuine trust inside one of the world's most connected startup ecosystems. You will own SimpleClosure's presence inside the SF VC and accelerator community: the platform teams, the program managers, the partners who quietly shepherd portfolio companies through hard transitions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be an integral part of our Partnerships team, supporting the SF market end-to-end: sourcing new partners, deepening existing ones, co-designing events, and building the kind of earned credibility that no outbound sequence can manufacture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>*</strong>Candidates <u>MUST</u> be located in the San Francisco Metro Area.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities </strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partnerships &amp; Pipeline</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a portfolio of VC fund and accelerator relationships from first outreach through activation and long-term engagement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Map the SF VC landscape: identify funds with the most portfolio distress exposure, surface platform leads and program managers, and prioritize by referral potential</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain referral pipelines with VC fund stakeholders, platform teams, accelerator program managers, startup attorneys, and ecosystem connectors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track all relationship activity, referral volume, and pipeline contribution in HubSpot — this is a real pipeline, and it needs to look like one</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the handoff loop: when a partner sends us a company, they should hear back fast and feel good about it</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ecosystem Presence</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Attend 3–5 Bay Area startup events per week — demo days, VC-hosted dinners, founder meetups, tech week gatherings, legal and accounting firm events</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build genuine relationships with: VC GPs/partners, finance and legal teams, and platform leads (especially those managing portfolio companies navigating wind-downs), accelerator program managers (YC, a16z, Soma Capital, First Round, etc.) and directly with founders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become the recognized SimpleClosure face in SF — the name that surfaces when the words \"shutdown\" or \"wind-down\" come up in conversation</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Events &amp; Programming</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support and co-own SimpleClosure's SF event programming alongside our Community team: founder dinners, VC roundtables, informal \"what to do when it's over\" conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify co-hosting and co-branding opportunities with ecosystem partners that extend reach without requiring a full production lift</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring back intel from every room you're in: what are founders worried about, what are VCs telling their portfolio, what language resonates</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Already embedded in the SF VC ecosystem — you have existing relationships at VC platform teams, accelerator programs, or startup law firms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5+ years in partnerships, BD, ecosystem, platform or community roles at a startup, financial services or VC</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized enough to run a real pipeline in CRM; not so transactional that you lose the trust that makes this work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine social energy — you are energized by events and people, not depleted by them. This is a personality fit, not a hustle requirement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator: warm in person, crisp in writing, responsive in Slack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with ambiguity and self-directed; you don't need a playbook to get moving</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have but not required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personal experience founding or shutting down a company — you know what this moment feels like from the inside</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing relationships at top SF-based funds and accelerator programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in fintech, legaltech, or professional services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience running or co-hosting branded ecosystem events</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation: OTE salary range $120,000 to $180,000 (this includes base pay and variable compensation)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote in San Francisco Bay area (with expectations of being in person for events)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT THE COMPANY\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nThis isn't a sales role.\n\nIt's a relationships role — built on genuine trust inside one of the world's most connected startup ecosystems. You will own SimpleClosure's presence inside the SF VC and accelerator community: the platform teams, the program managers, the partners who quietly shepherd portfolio companies through hard transitions.\n\nYou'll be an integral part of our Partnerships team, supporting the SF market end-to-end: sourcing new partners, deepening existing ones, co-designing events, and building the kind of earned credibility that no outbound sequence can manufacture.\n\n*Candidates MUST be located in the San Francisco Metro Area.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES \n\n - Partnerships & Pipeline\n   \n   - Own a portfolio of VC fund and accelerator relationships from first outreach through activation and long-term engagement\n   \n   - Map the SF VC landscape: identify funds with the most portfolio distress exposure, surface platform leads and program managers, and prioritize by referral potential\n   \n   - Build and maintain referral pipelines with VC fund stakeholders, platform teams, accelerator program managers, startup attorneys, and ecosystem connectors\n   \n   - Track all relationship activity, referral volume, and pipeline contribution in HubSpot — this is a real pipeline, and it needs to look like one\n   \n   - Own the handoff loop: when a partner sends us a company, they should hear back fast and feel good about it\n\n - Ecosystem Presence\n   \n   - Attend 3–5 Bay Area startup events per week — demo days, VC-hosted dinners, founder meetups, tech week gatherings, legal and accounting firm events\n   \n   - Build genuine relationships with: VC GPs/partners, finance and legal teams, and platform leads (especially those managing portfolio companies navigating wind-downs), accelerator program managers (YC, a16z, Soma Capital, First Round, etc.) and directly with founders.\n   \n   - Become the recognized SimpleClosure face in SF — the name that surfaces when the words \"shutdown\" or \"wind-down\" come up in conversation\n\n - Events & Programming\n   \n   - Support and co-own SimpleClosure's SF event programming alongside our Community team: founder dinners, VC roundtables, informal \"what to do when it's over\" conversations\n   \n   - Identify co-hosting and co-branding opportunities with ecosystem partners that extend reach without requiring a full production lift\n   \n   - Bring back intel from every room you're in: what are founders worried about, what are VCs telling their portfolio, what language resonates\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Already embedded in the SF VC ecosystem — you have existing relationships at VC platform teams, accelerator programs, or startup law firms\n\n - 3–5+ years in partnerships, BD, ecosystem, platform or community roles at a startup, financial services or VC\n\n - Organized enough to run a real pipeline in CRM; not so transactional that you lose the trust that makes this work\n\n - Genuine social energy — you are energized by events and people, not depleted by them. This is a personality fit, not a hustle requirement.\n\n - Strong communicator: warm in person, crisp in writing, responsive in Slack\n\n - Comfortable with ambiguity and self-directed; you don't need a playbook to get moving\n\nNice to have but not required:\n\n - Personal experience founding or shutting down a company — you know what this moment feels like from the inside\n\n - Existing relationships at top SF-based funds and accelerator programs\n\n - Background in fintech, legaltech, or professional services\n\n - Experience running or co-hosting branded ecosystem events\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Compensation: OTE salary range $120,000 to $180,000 (this includes base pay and variable compensation)\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Fully remote in San Francisco Bay area (with expectations of being in person for events)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"475dd0a3-0c86-44f4-a5c3-b9658bb40fa1","title":"SMB Account Executive","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Hybrid in New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}}},{"location":"Hybrid in Los Angeles","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T16:09:38.457+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/475dd0a3-0c86-44f4-a5c3-b9658bb40fa1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/475dd0a3-0c86-44f4-a5c3-b9658bb40fa1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Company Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a motivated SMB Account Executive to support our growing sales team and help expand our customer base. This is an excellent opportunity for someone early in their sales career who is eager to learn the full sales cycle, develop strong discovery and closing skills, and gain exposure to B2B SaaS sales in the legal and technology space.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll engage with prospective customers, support pipeline development, and work closely with senior sales leaders to close deals. You’ll receive hands-on coaching, clear performance goals, and a path for growth as the company scales.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities </strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist in identifying, researching, and qualifying prospective customers navigating business closures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct outbound and inbound outreach via phone, email, and social channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule and participate in discovery calls and product demonstrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support deal progression by managing follow-ups, next steps, and customer questions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate and up-to-date records in the CRM (e.g., HubSpot or Salesforce)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Marketing to improve lead quality and conversion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and share customer feedback to help refine sales messaging and product positioning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay informed on industry trends, customer needs, and competitive landscape</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently meet activity and pipeline goals while developing closing skills</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of closing experience in sales, customer-facing, or revenue-related roles (B2B SaaS or startup experience preferred)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interest in B2B sales, legal-tech, fintech, or startup environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience selling to founders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with a customer-first mindset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with outreach and engaging prospects via phone, email, and video</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coachable, curious, and eager to learn and grow in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM tools (HubSpot or Salesforce)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing, or a related field preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legal background or familiarity with corporate law or M&amp;A is a plus, but not required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation: OTE range for this role is $115,000–$130,000. Compensation is determined based on experience, qualifications, and geographic market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">New York or Los Angeles preferred; remote candidates will also be considered.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe are seeking a motivated SMB Account Executive to support our growing sales team and help expand our customer base. This is an excellent opportunity for someone early in their sales career who is eager to learn the full sales cycle, develop strong discovery and closing skills, and gain exposure to B2B SaaS sales in the legal and technology space.\n\nIn this role, you’ll engage with prospective customers, support pipeline development, and work closely with senior sales leaders to close deals. You’ll receive hands-on coaching, clear performance goals, and a path for growth as the company scales.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES \n\n - Assist in identifying, researching, and qualifying prospective customers navigating business closures\n\n - Conduct outbound and inbound outreach via phone, email, and social channels\n\n - Schedule and participate in discovery calls and product demonstrations\n\n - Support deal progression by managing follow-ups, next steps, and customer questions\n\n - Maintain accurate and up-to-date records in the CRM (e.g., HubSpot or Salesforce)\n\n - Collaborate with Marketing to improve lead quality and conversion\n\n - Gather and share customer feedback to help refine sales messaging and product positioning\n\n - Stay informed on industry trends, customer needs, and competitive landscape\n\n - Consistently meet activity and pipeline goals while developing closing skills\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 1–3 years of closing experience in sales, customer-facing, or revenue-related roles (B2B SaaS or startup experience preferred)\n\n - Strong interest in B2B sales, legal-tech, fintech, or startup environments\n\n - Experience selling to founders\n\n - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with a customer-first mindset\n\n - Comfortable with outreach and engaging prospects via phone, email, and video\n\n - Highly organized with the ability to manage multiple priorities\n\n - Coachable, curious, and eager to learn and grow in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Experience with CRM tools (HubSpot or Salesforce)\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing, or a related field preferred\n\n - Legal background or familiarity with corporate law or M&A is a plus, but not required\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Compensation: OTE range for this role is $115,000–$130,000. Compensation is determined based on experience, qualifications, and geographic market.\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\n - New York or Los Angeles preferred; remote candidates will also be considered.\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.\n\nWe do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e872cbdd-9ccf-4e18-a8eb-f7e7b8dcc785","title":"Product Manager, Product Partnerships - Asset Hub","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T19:49:45.808+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/e872cbdd-9ccf-4e18-a8eb-f7e7b8dcc785","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/e872cbdd-9ccf-4e18-a8eb-f7e7b8dcc785/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>Company Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we're headed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company's life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Job Overview</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a mid-senior Product Manager to own Product for Asset Hub, SimpleClosure's marketplace for the assets left behind when a company shuts down — codebases, workspaces, proprietary data, and talent. Our buyers include some of the top foundation model labs, RL environment providers, and AI agent builders in the world, who rely on Asset Hub as a differentiated source of proprietary data and talent they can't get anywhere else. You'll build the tools and products that power asset selling and buying, improve SimpleClosure's internal processes through technology, and find, manage, and implement partners who let us offer more types of asset value recovery and liquidation. Your work spans Asset Hub's full surface area — the buyer portal for codebases and workspaces, domains, and TalentPipe — so partnership experience is essential. This role reports to Doron Samish, Director of Product, and sits within a dedicated Asset Hub team with a dotted line to Itai Bengal, GM of Asset Hub.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the tools and products that power asset selling and buying across Asset Hub’s full surface area — the buyer portal (codebases, workspaces), domains, physical assets, TalentPipe, and future asset types.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify manual, internal processes (asset intake, cataloging, pricing, deal tracking) and replace them with tooling that lets the team scale without adding headcount.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source, evaluate, negotiate, and manage external partners that let SimpleClosure offer more types of asset value recovery and liquidation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Turn each partnership into a working product and process, not just a signed agreement — own the integration end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with engineering, legal/compliance, RevOps, and GTM to ship and operationalize this work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of product management experience, including shipping B2B, platform, or marketplace products end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience building or managing partnerships — sourcing partners, structuring the commercial/product relationship, and shipping the resulting integration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort owning a broad, sometimes ambiguous surface area and prioritizing ruthlessly across a primary focus and multiple adjacent products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with technical or enterprise buyers and sales-assisted, quote-driven motions — not just self-serve.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional operator, with experience partnering across engineering, legal, and go-to-market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward building 0-to-1 and turning ad hoc, manual work into repeatable systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have: experience in data licensing, data marketplaces, M&amp;A/data-room products, domain sales/aftermarket, or talent marketplaces.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Salary: $130,000-$170,000, depending on experience level and location</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (currently 2 days per week in office)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.\n\nAs the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we're headed.\n\nJoining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company's life.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe're looking for a mid-senior Product Manager to own Product for Asset Hub, SimpleClosure's marketplace for the assets left behind when a company shuts down — codebases, workspaces, proprietary data, and talent. Our buyers include some of the top foundation model labs, RL environment providers, and AI agent builders in the world, who rely on Asset Hub as a differentiated source of proprietary data and talent they can't get anywhere else. You'll build the tools and products that power asset selling and buying, improve SimpleClosure's internal processes through technology, and find, manage, and implement partners who let us offer more types of asset value recovery and liquidation. Your work spans Asset Hub's full surface area — the buyer portal for codebases and workspaces, domains, and TalentPipe — so partnership experience is essential. This role reports to Doron Samish, Director of Product, and sits within a dedicated Asset Hub team with a dotted line to Itai Bengal, GM of Asset Hub.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Build the tools and products that power asset selling and buying across Asset Hub’s full surface area — the buyer portal (codebases, workspaces), domains, physical assets, TalentPipe, and future asset types.\n\n - Identify manual, internal processes (asset intake, cataloging, pricing, deal tracking) and replace them with tooling that lets the team scale without adding headcount.\n\n - Source, evaluate, negotiate, and manage external partners that let SimpleClosure offer more types of asset value recovery and liquidation.\n\n - Turn each partnership into a working product and process, not just a signed agreement — own the integration end-to-end.\n\n - Partner closely with engineering, legal/compliance, RevOps, and GTM to ship and operationalize this work.\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 3+ years of product management experience, including shipping B2B, platform, or marketplace products end-to-end.\n\n - Direct experience building or managing partnerships — sourcing partners, structuring the commercial/product relationship, and shipping the resulting integration.\n\n - Comfort owning a broad, sometimes ambiguous surface area and prioritizing ruthlessly across a primary focus and multiple adjacent products.\n\n - Experience working with technical or enterprise buyers and sales-assisted, quote-driven motions — not just self-serve.\n\n - Strong cross-functional operator, with experience partnering across engineering, legal, and go-to-market.\n\n - A bias toward building 0-to-1 and turning ad hoc, manual work into repeatable systems.\n\n - Nice to have: experience in data licensing, data marketplaces, M&A/data-room products, domain sales/aftermarket, or talent marketplaces.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Base Salary: $130,000-$170,000, depending on experience level and location\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (currently 2 days per week in office)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9b173513-600a-4caa-8451-5c2e336bd8b8","title":"Strategic AI Partnerships & BD Lead - Asset Hub","department":"Asset Hub","team":"Asset Hub","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Remote in San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}},{"location":"Hybrid in Los Angeles","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T20:26:50.548+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/9b173513-600a-4caa-8451-5c2e336bd8b8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/9b173513-600a-4caa-8451-5c2e336bd8b8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>Company Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we're headed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company's life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Job Overview</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring a <strong>Strategic AI Partnerships &amp; BD Lead</strong> to help us expand, and own some of our top AI partners and asset buyers. You’ll originate, structure, and grow the partnerships that turn our unique supply of assets into recurring licensing revenue — building relationships with AI labs and the companies that serve them, understanding exactly what they need for pre- and post-training, and translating that demand back into how we source and package supply. This is a senior, high-autonomy role for someone who knows the AI data and training ecosystem inside and out and can operate credibly with the people building frontier models.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and grow buyer-side relationships across frontier labs, RL environment builders, data and evaluation vendors, labeling firms, and enterprise AI teams — from first conversation through signed, recurring licensing deals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Originate new demand: identify which organizations need which assets — pre-training corpora, post-training and RL data, codebases, workspace data, specialized datasets — and open the door.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structure and negotiate commercial terms — licensing structures, exclusivity, rights, and pricing, including MSAs and order forms — in close partnership with legal.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the voice of the buyer internally: translate what labs actually need into how we source, qualify, and package supply, working with product, supply, and engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay ahead of a fast-moving market — training methods, evolving data needs, and the competitive landscape of labeling, RLE, and data vendors — and shape our commercial strategy accordingly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent AssetHub credibly with senior technical and commercial stakeholders at labs and partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the repeatable playbook and infrastructure — pipeline, process, and materials — that lets buyer-side partnerships scale.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep, current knowledge of the AI data and model-training ecosystem — both pre-training and post-training / RL — and how labs actually acquire and use data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience at an AI lab, an RL environment or data/evaluation company, or in a function that sold to or partnered with those companies (BD, partnerships, GTM, or commercial).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record originating and closing complex, high-value partnerships or commercial deals, ideally involving data or technical products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort structuring and negotiating licensing and commercial terms alongside legal — exclusivity, rights, and pricing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent enough in the technical substance to earn credibility with researchers and technical buyers, without needing to be an engineer.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An existing network across labs, RLE / data companies, or the broader AI ecosystem is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A self-starter who is comfortable with ambiguity and energized by building a young, fast-moving business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A senior operator — typically 7+ years in BD, partnerships, or commercial roles, with meaningful time in or adjacent to the AI / ML ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in (or willing to work hybrid from) the Los Angeles, San Francisco, or New York metro.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation package consisting of a base salary and performance-based variable component.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City (Midtown), Los Angeles (Santa Monica), or San Francisco (remote but must be in SF)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.\n\nAs the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we're headed.\n\nJoining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company's life.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re hiring a Strategic AI Partnerships & BD Lead to help us expand, and own some of our top AI partners and asset buyers. You’ll originate, structure, and grow the partnerships that turn our unique supply of assets into recurring licensing revenue — building relationships with AI labs and the companies that serve them, understanding exactly what they need for pre- and post-training, and translating that demand back into how we source and package supply. This is a senior, high-autonomy role for someone who knows the AI data and training ecosystem inside and out and can operate credibly with the people building frontier models.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Own and grow buyer-side relationships across frontier labs, RL environment builders, data and evaluation vendors, labeling firms, and enterprise AI teams — from first conversation through signed, recurring licensing deals.\n\n - Originate new demand: identify which organizations need which assets — pre-training corpora, post-training and RL data, codebases, workspace data, specialized datasets — and open the door.\n\n - Structure and negotiate commercial terms — licensing structures, exclusivity, rights, and pricing, including MSAs and order forms — in close partnership with legal.\n\n - Be the voice of the buyer internally: translate what labs actually need into how we source, qualify, and package supply, working with product, supply, and engineering.\n\n - Stay ahead of a fast-moving market — training methods, evolving data needs, and the competitive landscape of labeling, RLE, and data vendors — and shape our commercial strategy accordingly.\n\n - Represent AssetHub credibly with senior technical and commercial stakeholders at labs and partners.\n\n - Build the repeatable playbook and infrastructure — pipeline, process, and materials — that lets buyer-side partnerships scale.\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Deep, current knowledge of the AI data and model-training ecosystem — both pre-training and post-training / RL — and how labs actually acquire and use data.\n\n - Experience at an AI lab, an RL environment or data/evaluation company, or in a function that sold to or partnered with those companies (BD, partnerships, GTM, or commercial).\n\n - A track record originating and closing complex, high-value partnerships or commercial deals, ideally involving data or technical products.\n\n - Comfort structuring and negotiating licensing and commercial terms alongside legal — exclusivity, rights, and pricing.\n\n - Fluent enough in the technical substance to earn credibility with researchers and technical buyers, without needing to be an engineer.\n\n - An existing network across labs, RLE / data companies, or the broader AI ecosystem is a strong plus.\n\n - A self-starter who is comfortable with ambiguity and energized by building a young, fast-moving business.\n\n - A senior operator — typically 7+ years in BD, partnerships, or commercial roles, with meaningful time in or adjacent to the AI / ML ecosystem.\n\n - Based in (or willing to work hybrid from) the Los Angeles, San Francisco, or New York metro.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Competitive compensation package consisting of a base salary and performance-based variable component.\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City (Midtown), Los Angeles (Santa Monica), or San Francisco (remote but must be in SF)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"036aaf67-6713-42fe-a82d-007608af713f","title":"Legal Counsel ","department":"Legal","team":"Legal","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in Los Angeles","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Hybrid in New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T20:45:29.604+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/036aaf67-6713-42fe-a82d-007608af713f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/036aaf67-6713-42fe-a82d-007608af713f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>Company Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Job Overview</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a business-minded Legal Counsel to join our legal team as a generalist, working cross-functionally across sales, operations, customer success, and commercial partnerships. This person will be the second in-house attorney on staff and will play a key role in building out a legal function that touches dissolution operations, commercial contracting, licensing, vendor management, and regulatory compliance across multiple jurisdictions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role goes beyond a traditional in-house counsel role. You'll be responsible for customer-facing legal communications, sales support, and deal-risk reviews while building toward broader coverage across the full business. You should feel comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment and exercising independent judgment on legal questions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide practical, business-oriented legal advice to teams across the organization, including sales, operations, customer success, marketing, engineering and partnerships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Draft, review, and negotiate a range of commercial agreements, including licensing, vendor, and partner contracts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise the sales team on legal and regulatory questions arising in the customer acquisition process, including joining prospect and customer calls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customer-facing legal communications and escalations across the dissolution lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct legal research and analysis to support expansion into new U.S. jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and assess legal risks across business initiatives and develop practical mitigation strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help build and improve internal templates, playbooks, and processes that enable teams to move faster while managing risk</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review customer-facing and marketing materials for legal and regulatory compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with outside counsel on specialized matters as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take on additional projects and priorities as the business scales</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">JD from an ABA-accredited law school; active membership in good standing with at least one U.S. state bar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2-4 years of legal experience, ideally a mix of law firm and in-house</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial instincts: comfortable reviewing contracts, spotting risk, and advising business teams without over-lawyering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communicator who can translate complex legal concepts into clear, actionable guidance for non-legal stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail-oriented with strong drafting skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating independently in a fast-paced startup environment with limited supervision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in or exposure to corporate dissolution, licensing or data privacy is a plus but not required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in corporate transactions, commercial contracting, or general in-house practice is a plus but not required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Salary: $125,000 - $165,000 depending on experience level and location</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hybrid work environment in NY (Midtown) or Los Angeles (Santa Monica)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe're looking for a business-minded Legal Counsel to join our legal team as a generalist, working cross-functionally across sales, operations, customer success, and commercial partnerships. This person will be the second in-house attorney on staff and will play a key role in building out a legal function that touches dissolution operations, commercial contracting, licensing, vendor management, and regulatory compliance across multiple jurisdictions.\n\nThis role goes beyond a traditional in-house counsel role. You'll be responsible for customer-facing legal communications, sales support, and deal-risk reviews while building toward broader coverage across the full business. You should feel comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment and exercising independent judgment on legal questions.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Provide practical, business-oriented legal advice to teams across the organization, including sales, operations, customer success, marketing, engineering and partnerships\n\n - Draft, review, and negotiate a range of commercial agreements, including licensing, vendor, and partner contracts\n\n - Advise the sales team on legal and regulatory questions arising in the customer acquisition process, including joining prospect and customer calls\n\n - Support customer-facing legal communications and escalations across the dissolution lifecycle\n\n - Conduct legal research and analysis to support expansion into new U.S. jurisdictions\n\n - Identify and assess legal risks across business initiatives and develop practical mitigation strategies\n\n - Help build and improve internal templates, playbooks, and processes that enable teams to move faster while managing risk\n\n - Review customer-facing and marketing materials for legal and regulatory compliance\n\n - Coordinate with outside counsel on specialized matters as needed\n\n - Take on additional projects and priorities as the business scales\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - JD from an ABA-accredited law school; active membership in good standing with at least one U.S. state bar\n\n - 2-4 years of legal experience, ideally a mix of law firm and in-house\n\n - Strong commercial instincts: comfortable reviewing contracts, spotting risk, and advising business teams without over-lawyering\n\n - Excellent communicator who can translate complex legal concepts into clear, actionable guidance for non-legal stakeholders\n\n - Detail-oriented with strong drafting skills\n\n - Comfortable operating independently in a fast-paced startup environment with limited supervision\n\n - Interest in or exposure to corporate dissolution, licensing or data privacy is a plus but not required\n\n - Prior experience in corporate transactions, commercial contracting, or general in-house practice is a plus but not required\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Base Salary: $125,000 - $165,000 depending on experience level and location\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Hybrid work environment in NY (Midtown) or Los Angeles (Santa Monica)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"614c05ea-148b-4813-9639-54e7b313c1ee","title":"AI/ML Engineer, RL Environments - Asset Hub","department":"Asset Hub","team":"Asset Hub","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T00:54:48.475+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/614c05ea-148b-4813-9639-54e7b313c1ee","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/614c05ea-148b-4813-9639-54e7b313c1ee/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Company Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don’t end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we’re headed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company’s life.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SimpleClosure is seeking an AI/ML Engineer to turn Asset Hub’s one-of-a-kind inventory, and existing AI buyer relationships, into high-value AI-training products. When companies shut down, we acquire the real assets they built — production codebases, workspaces, and databases. Your job is to find the opportunities hidden in that inventory and build them: transforming real-world assets into derivative works — reinforcement-learning environments, agentic task suites, evaluations and verifiers, and training datasets — that are far more valuable to the AI labs, RL-environment providers, and agent builders who already buy from us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a hands-on building role for someone who comes from the RL-environments and AI-training world and has actually created environments and products used to train or evaluate models — that background is essential. You’ll prototype fast, then harden what works into repeatable pipelines, working in a small, dedicated Asset Hub pod alongside product, engineering, and the GM of Asset Hub.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>*Candidates MUST be located in the New York City Metro area.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take Asset Hub’s unique real-world assets — production codebases, workspaces, and databases — and identify how each can become a high-value AI-training product: RL environments, agentic task suites, evals and verifiers, benchmarks, and fine-tuning or trajectory datasets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build the pipeline that turns a raw asset into a derivative work: repository ingestion, test harnessing, commit-mining for task extraction, Docker/sandbox reproducibility, verifier and reward scripts, and QA tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Wrap real data in interactive environments — sandboxed application state, MCP servers, and browser/Playwright layers — that buyers can train and evaluate agents against.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spot the commercial opportunity in the inventory: which assets map to current lab and RLE demand, and what derivative product maximizes their value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prototype quickly, then harden the best ideas into repeatable, scalable pipelines so derivative-work creation isn’t one-off.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Asset Hub buyer/BD side and directly with technical stakeholders at labs and RLE buyers to shape what we build to their training needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with sensitive material — codebases, workspace exports, and proprietary datasets — with strong attention to security, privacy, licensing, and PII handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, well-tested code and use AI tooling to move faster; collaborate closely with product, engineering, and the GM of Asset Hub.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>RL-environments / AI-training background (critical): </strong>you’ve built RL environments and/or products used to train or evaluate models — environments, agentic task suites, evals, benchmarks, or verifiers. This is the core requirement, not a nice-to-have.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>4–8 years of engineering experience, with meaningful time in the RL-environments, AI-training-data, or model-evaluation ecosystem (at a lab, an RLE/eval company, or a team that shipped training environments or products).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Core engineering: </strong>strong Python, containers (Docker), and CI/test infrastructure; comfort building reproducible sandboxes from messy real-world code and data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evals &amp; verification: </strong>familiarity with LLM evaluation and agent harnesses (SWE-bench-style setups, Verifiers, HUD, or similar) and with verifier/reward design, including resistance to reward hacking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ownership: </strong>a builder’s temperament — takes projects from concept to production, works scrappily (sometimes alongside contractors), and thrives in ambiguity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication: </strong>a clear communicator who can be a credible technical face to lab and RLE researchers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to have: </strong>contributions to public benchmarks or eval frameworks; experience with post-training / fine-tuning data; simulation or frontend skills (MCP, Playwright) for world-building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education: </strong>Bachelor’s or Master’s in Computer Science, Machine Learning, or a related field — or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Management: </strong>experience building and managing a team of engineers, a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation package consisting of a base salary and performance-based variable component.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (currently 2 days per week in office)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we’re looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don’t end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We go a step further, helping companies sell their remaining assets and return the most value to their stakeholders, through our Asset Hub.\n\nAs the leading platform for company shutdowns, we have something no one else does: a continuous, proprietary flow of companies winding down, and the assets they built along the way. Our buyers span the top AI labs, RL environment providers, vertical and enterprise agent builders, VCs and deal-flow partners, domain marketplaces, and much more. Dissolution is our wedge; the marketplace is a big part of where we’re headed.\n\nJoining our Asset Hub team means helping to define a new category from the ground up, working on complex, high-stakes problems, and building the products and processes that guide founders through one of the most consequential moments in a company’s life.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nSimpleClosure is seeking an AI/ML Engineer to turn Asset Hub’s one-of-a-kind inventory, and existing AI buyer relationships, into high-value AI-training products. When companies shut down, we acquire the real assets they built — production codebases, workspaces, and databases. Your job is to find the opportunities hidden in that inventory and build them: transforming real-world assets into derivative works — reinforcement-learning environments, agentic task suites, evaluations and verifiers, and training datasets — that are far more valuable to the AI labs, RL-environment providers, and agent builders who already buy from us.\n\nThis is a hands-on building role for someone who comes from the RL-environments and AI-training world and has actually created environments and products used to train or evaluate models — that background is essential. You’ll prototype fast, then harden what works into repeatable pipelines, working in a small, dedicated Asset Hub pod alongside product, engineering, and the GM of Asset Hub.\n\n*Candidates MUST be located in the New York City Metro area.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Take Asset Hub’s unique real-world assets — production codebases, workspaces, and databases — and identify how each can become a high-value AI-training product: RL environments, agentic task suites, evals and verifiers, benchmarks, and fine-tuning or trajectory datasets.\n\n - Design and build the pipeline that turns a raw asset into a derivative work: repository ingestion, test harnessing, commit-mining for task extraction, Docker/sandbox reproducibility, verifier and reward scripts, and QA tooling.\n\n - Wrap real data in interactive environments — sandboxed application state, MCP servers, and browser/Playwright layers — that buyers can train and evaluate agents against.\n\n - Spot the commercial opportunity in the inventory: which assets map to current lab and RLE demand, and what derivative product maximizes their value.\n\n - Prototype quickly, then harden the best ideas into repeatable, scalable pipelines so derivative-work creation isn’t one-off.\n\n - Partner with the Asset Hub buyer/BD side and directly with technical stakeholders at labs and RLE buyers to shape what we build to their training needs.\n\n - Work with sensitive material — codebases, workspace exports, and proprietary datasets — with strong attention to security, privacy, licensing, and PII handling.\n\n - Write clean, well-tested code and use AI tooling to move faster; collaborate closely with product, engineering, and the GM of Asset Hub.\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - RL-environments / AI-training background (critical): you’ve built RL environments and/or products used to train or evaluate models — environments, agentic task suites, evals, benchmarks, or verifiers. This is the core requirement, not a nice-to-have.\n\n - Experience: 4–8 years of engineering experience, with meaningful time in the RL-environments, AI-training-data, or model-evaluation ecosystem (at a lab, an RLE/eval company, or a team that shipped training environments or products).\n\n - Core engineering: strong Python, containers (Docker), and CI/test infrastructure; comfort building reproducible sandboxes from messy real-world code and data.\n\n - Evals & verification: familiarity with LLM evaluation and agent harnesses (SWE-bench-style setups, Verifiers, HUD, or similar) and with verifier/reward design, including resistance to reward hacking.\n\n - Ownership: a builder’s temperament — takes projects from concept to production, works scrappily (sometimes alongside contractors), and thrives in ambiguity.\n\n - Communication: a clear communicator who can be a credible technical face to lab and RLE researchers.\n\n - Nice to have: contributions to public benchmarks or eval frameworks; experience with post-training / fine-tuning data; simulation or frontend skills (MCP, Playwright) for world-building.\n\n - Education: Bachelor’s or Master’s in Computer Science, Machine Learning, or a related field — or equivalent practical experience.\n\n - Team Management: experience building and managing a team of engineers, a plus.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Competitive compensation package consisting of a base salary and performance-based variable component.\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (currently 2 days per week in office)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we’re looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process. We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"308a86df-752c-49c9-bafb-e4fc5958d1eb","title":"Senior Product Partnerships Manager","department":"Partnerships","team":"Partnerships","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in Los Angeles","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Hybrid in New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}}},{"location":"Remote in San Francisco","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T20:37:55.843+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/308a86df-752c-49c9-bafb-e4fc5958d1eb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/308a86df-752c-49c9-bafb-e4fc5958d1eb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Company Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Senior Product Partnerships Manager to own and scale SimpleClosure's partner ecosystem. This is one of the highest-leverage roles at the company: you'll identify, structure, and close major partnerships that have the potential to inflect our growth curve and reshape our entire revenue trajectory.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This person builds deep, integrated relationships — not a traditional channel or referral partnerships role, but one focused on high-impact deals that embed SimpleClosure into the products and platforms founders already rely on. Done right, these partnerships unlock durable recurring revenue and cement SimpleClosure as an essential part of the founder journey, from startup to shutdown.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll operate cross-functionally at the highest level, working directly with the CEO and partnering closely with R&amp;D and GTM to identify, structure, and execute strategic partnerships with technology platforms, financial services, and ecosystems that touch founders at key inflection points.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">*Ideal candidates MUST be located in New York City, San Francisco, or Los Angeles metro areas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and nurture relationships with senior decision-makers across key technology platforms, financial institutions, and ecosystem partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent SimpleClosure as a trusted, high-value partner that helps others better serve founders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead commercial negotiations to create win-win partnerships that incentivize adoption and drive mutual success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure SimpleClosure is seamlessly embedded into partner workflows and customer experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work hand-in-hand with Product, GTM, and Operations to scope, prioritize, and execute integrations that create measurable impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use customer and partner data signals to continuously optimize how partnerships deliver value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adhere to a clear, data-informed strategy for identifying and prioritizing strategic product partnerships that drive recurring revenue and scalable growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate potential integrations and partnership models, ensuring strong alignment with product and business goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and track key partnership KPIs, including revenue contribution, adoption metrics, and customer experience improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously refine the partnership model to scale with SimpleClosure’s growth trajectory.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Professional Experience &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experienced: 6+ years business development, strategic partnerships or ecosystem development, ideally within B2B SaaS, fintech, or integrated product environments. Experience working with Payroll providers is not required, but a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technically Fluent: You can work with product and technical teams to identify integration opportunities and understand API-based collaboration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relationship-Oriented: You’re skilled at building trust with senior stakeholders and navigating complex organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deal-Minded: Strong commercial negotiation skills with a track record of structuring win-win partnerships across complex (sometimes multi-threaded) legal contracts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Entrepreneurial: You thrive in fast-moving, ambiguous environments and can balance strategy with hands-on execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation: OTE salary range $160,000 to $230,000 (this includes base pay and variable compensation)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City (Midtown), Los Angeles (Santa Monica), or San Francisco (remote but based in SF)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.<br /></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe're looking for a Senior Product Partnerships Manager to own and scale SimpleClosure's partner ecosystem. This is one of the highest-leverage roles at the company: you'll identify, structure, and close major partnerships that have the potential to inflect our growth curve and reshape our entire revenue trajectory.\n\nThis person builds deep, integrated relationships — not a traditional channel or referral partnerships role, but one focused on high-impact deals that embed SimpleClosure into the products and platforms founders already rely on. Done right, these partnerships unlock durable recurring revenue and cement SimpleClosure as an essential part of the founder journey, from startup to shutdown.\n\nYou'll operate cross-functionally at the highest level, working directly with the CEO and partnering closely with R&D and GTM to identify, structure, and execute strategic partnerships with technology platforms, financial services, and ecosystems that touch founders at key inflection points.\n\n*Ideal candidates MUST be located in New York City, San Francisco, or Los Angeles metro areas.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Develop and nurture relationships with senior decision-makers across key technology platforms, financial institutions, and ecosystem partners.\n\n - Represent SimpleClosure as a trusted, high-value partner that helps others better serve founders.\n\n - Lead commercial negotiations to create win-win partnerships that incentivize adoption and drive mutual success.\n\n - Ensure SimpleClosure is seamlessly embedded into partner workflows and customer experiences.\n\n - Work hand-in-hand with Product, GTM, and Operations to scope, prioritize, and execute integrations that create measurable impact.\n\n - Use customer and partner data signals to continuously optimize how partnerships deliver value.\n\n - Adhere to a clear, data-informed strategy for identifying and prioritizing strategic product partnerships that drive recurring revenue and scalable growth.\n\n - Evaluate potential integrations and partnership models, ensuring strong alignment with product and business goals.\n\n - Define and track key partnership KPIs, including revenue contribution, adoption metrics, and customer experience improvements.\n\n - Continuously refine the partnership model to scale with SimpleClosure’s growth trajectory.\n   \n   \n\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Experienced: 6+ years business development, strategic partnerships or ecosystem development, ideally within B2B SaaS, fintech, or integrated product environments. Experience working with Payroll providers is not required, but a plus.\n\n - Technically Fluent: You can work with product and technical teams to identify integration opportunities and understand API-based collaboration.\n\n - Relationship-Oriented: You’re skilled at building trust with senior stakeholders and navigating complex organizations.\n\n - Deal-Minded: Strong commercial negotiation skills with a track record of structuring win-win partnerships across complex (sometimes multi-threaded) legal contracts.\n\n - Entrepreneurial: You thrive in fast-moving, ambiguous environments and can balance strategy with hands-on execution.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Compensation: OTE salary range $160,000 to $230,000 (this includes base pay and variable compensation)\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City (Midtown), Los Angeles (Santa Monica), or San Francisco (remote but based in SF)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.\n\nWe do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3d29b324-ee7c-4f47-b9a5-f9d1276f9ee5","title":"General Job Application","department":"General","team":"General","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Hybrid in Los Angeles","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T20:34:35.499+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/3d29b324-ee7c-4f47-b9a5-f9d1276f9ee5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/3d29b324-ee7c-4f47-b9a5-f9d1276f9ee5/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>General application</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Don't see a role that's the right fit? Submit your resume here, and we'll reach out if a relevant opportunity comes up in the future.</p>","descriptionPlain":"GENERAL APPLICATION\n\nDon't see a role that's the right fit? Submit your resume here, and we'll reach out if a relevant opportunity comes up in the future.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"665cd5c9-9a51-41c4-a3c1-aa440d84c127","title":"Director of Marketing","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in NY or LA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T04:04:25.119+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York or California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York or Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/665cd5c9-9a51-41c4-a3c1-aa440d84c127","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/665cd5c9-9a51-41c4-a3c1-aa440d84c127/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>Company Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Job Overview</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring a Director of Marketing to own and operate the full marketing engine at SimpleClosure. This is a senior, execution-heavy leadership role for someone who thrives in structure, clarity, and accountability.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will translate company strategy into repeatable marketing systems that drive predictable, measurable growth. This is not a brand-only or vision-only role, it is a systems-oriented, performance-accountable role with full ownership of how marketing operates day to day, from people and process to performance and planning.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Marketing at SimpleClosure is central to our ability to deliver predictable, durable growth. The Director of Marketing will play a critical role in turning momentum into a system, and ensuring the company is positioned to compound growth over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll report to the Head of GTM and Revenue.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><strong>Marketing Operations &amp; Execution</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own day-to-day marketing execution across all channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, document, and continuously improve marketing processes and workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish operating cadence, prioritization frameworks, and delivery discipline</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure initiatives ship on time and meet a high quality bar</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Performance &amp; Commercial Accountability</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own marketing KPIs across the funnel (top-of-funnel through revenue impact)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be accountable for performance, efficiency, and ROI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with RevOps to ensure clean attribution, reporting, and forecasting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make data-backed decisions and course corrections</p></li></ul><h3><strong>People Leadership</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, manage, and develop the marketing team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create clarity around roles, ownership, and expectations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run effective planning, feedback, and performance cycles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scale the team thoughtfully as the business grows</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Brand &amp; PR</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own SimpleClosure’s brand from strategy through execution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage PR strategy, press relationships, and narrative development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure consistent, high-quality brand expression across all touchpoints</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with leadership on messaging and external positioning</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Product Marketing</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own positioning, messaging, and go-to-market strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Sales to ensure alignment and clarity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop enablement materials, narratives, and competitive differentiation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Performance Marketing, Lifecycle &amp; Growth Ops</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own paid channels, lifecycle marketing, and conversion optimization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build scalable acquisition and nurture systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize CAC, conversion rates, and funnel efficiency<br />Ensure operational excellence across campaign execution</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Events &amp; Swag</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own strategy and execution for industry, partner, and owned events</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure experiential marketing reinforces brand and drives outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage swag and physical brand touchpoints with intention and quality</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Planning, Analytics &amp; Infrastructure</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own long-term marketing planning and roadmap development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reporting infrastructure and dashboards for leadership visibility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish measurement frameworks to guide strategy and investment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously evaluate and evolve the marketing tech stack</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong></h2><h3><strong>Required Traits &amp; Strengths</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational rigor, structure, and planning discipline</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of owning performance and being held accountable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading teams across complex, multi-threaded initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort owning brand and PR end-to-end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep analytical mindset with the ability to turn data into strategy</p></li></ul><h3><strong>This Role Is a Great Fit If You…</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Love building systems and processes that scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are energized by execution and operational excellence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enjoy leading teams and creating clarity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Think in terms of inputs, outputs, and measurable impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prefer ownership over influence</p></li></ul><h3><strong>This Role Is Not</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A “big ideas only” role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An early-stage generalist role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A pure brand or content role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A skunkworks or experimentation-only role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Salary: $140,000 to $200,000, depending on experience level and location</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hybrid work environment in New York or Los Angeles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nWe’re hiring a Director of Marketing to own and operate the full marketing engine at SimpleClosure. This is a senior, execution-heavy leadership role for someone who thrives in structure, clarity, and accountability.\n\nYou will translate company strategy into repeatable marketing systems that drive predictable, measurable growth. This is not a brand-only or vision-only role, it is a systems-oriented, performance-accountable role with full ownership of how marketing operates day to day, from people and process to performance and planning.\n\nMarketing at SimpleClosure is central to our ability to deliver predictable, durable growth. The Director of Marketing will play a critical role in turning momentum into a system, and ensuring the company is positioned to compound growth over time.\n\nYou’ll report to the Head of GTM and Revenue.\n\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n\nMARKETING OPERATIONS & EXECUTION\n\n - Own day-to-day marketing execution across all channels\n\n - Build, document, and continuously improve marketing processes and workflows\n\n - Establish operating cadence, prioritization frameworks, and delivery discipline\n\n - Ensure initiatives ship on time and meet a high quality bar\n\n\nPERFORMANCE & COMMERCIAL ACCOUNTABILITY\n\n - Own marketing KPIs across the funnel (top-of-funnel through revenue impact)\n\n - Be accountable for performance, efficiency, and ROI\n\n - Partner with RevOps to ensure clean attribution, reporting, and forecasting\n\n - Make data-backed decisions and course corrections\n\n\nPEOPLE LEADERSHIP\n\n - Lead, manage, and develop the marketing team\n\n - Create clarity around roles, ownership, and expectations\n\n - Run effective planning, feedback, and performance cycles\n\n - Scale the team thoughtfully as the business grows\n\n\nBRAND & PR\n\n - Own SimpleClosure’s brand from strategy through execution\n\n - Manage PR strategy, press relationships, and narrative development\n\n - Ensure consistent, high-quality brand expression across all touchpoints\n\n - Partner with leadership on messaging and external positioning\n\n\nPRODUCT MARKETING\n\n - Own positioning, messaging, and go-to-market strategy\n\n - Partner with Product and Sales to ensure alignment and clarity\n\n - Develop enablement materials, narratives, and competitive differentiation\n\n\nPERFORMANCE MARKETING, LIFECYCLE & GROWTH OPS\n\n - Own paid channels, lifecycle marketing, and conversion optimization\n\n - Build scalable acquisition and nurture systems\n\n - Optimize CAC, conversion rates, and funnel efficiency\n   Ensure operational excellence across campaign execution\n\n\nEVENTS & SWAG\n\n - Own strategy and execution for industry, partner, and owned events\n\n - Ensure experiential marketing reinforces brand and drives outcomes\n\n - Manage swag and physical brand touchpoints with intention and quality\n\n\nPLANNING, ANALYTICS & INFRASTRUCTURE\n\n - Own long-term marketing planning and roadmap development\n\n - Build reporting infrastructure and dashboards for leadership visibility\n\n - Establish measurement frameworks to guide strategy and investment\n\n - Continuously evaluate and evolve the marketing tech stack\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n\nREQUIRED TRAITS & STRENGTHS\n\n - Strong operational rigor, structure, and planning discipline\n\n - Proven track record of owning performance and being held accountable\n\n - Experience leading teams across complex, multi-threaded initiatives\n\n - Comfort owning brand and PR end-to-end\n\n - Deep analytical mindset with the ability to turn data into strategy\n\n\nTHIS ROLE IS A GREAT FIT IF YOU…\n\n - Love building systems and processes that scale\n\n - Are energized by execution and operational excellence\n\n - Enjoy leading teams and creating clarity\n\n - Think in terms of inputs, outputs, and measurable impact\n\n - Prefer ownership over influence\n\n\nTHIS ROLE IS NOT\n\n - A “big ideas only” role\n\n - An early-stage generalist role\n\n - A pure brand or content role\n\n - A skunkworks or experimentation-only role\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Base Salary: $140,000 to $200,000, depending on experience level and location\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Flexible hybrid work environment in New York or Los Angeles\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.\n\nWe do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"31e9ea72-90b3-4f07-8ee4-78505bc4d495","title":"Senior Infrastructure Engineer - Asset Hub","department":"Asset Hub","team":"Asset Hub","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Hybrid in New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T22:14:19.466+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/31e9ea72-90b3-4f07-8ee4-78505bc4d495","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/simpleclosure/31e9ea72-90b3-4f07-8ee4-78505bc4d495/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>Company Overview</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Having raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Job Overview</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SimpleClosure is seeking an experienced Infrastructure Engineer to join Asset Hub, SimpleClosure's marketplace for the assets left behind when a company shuts down, including codebases, workspaces, proprietary data, and talent. Our buyers include some of the top foundation model labs, RL environment providers, and AI agent builders in the world, who rely on Asset Hub as a differentiated source of proprietary data and talent they can't get anywhere else. In this role, you’ll take the lead in building novel systems from the ground up that support digital asset acquisition, preparation and delivery. You’ll work closely with leadership, product, and design to ensure we deliver high-quality, scalable, and maintainable solutions. This position is hybrid in NYC and reports directly to the CTO.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the technical design, development, and delivery of complex features from concept to deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor and guide other engineers, promoting strong engineering practices and continuous learning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect scalable, maintainable systems across the stack, ensuring alignment with business goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally to translate product requirements into technical solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct and lead code reviews to maintain quality, performance, and security standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and configure the protective systems, processes, software, and networks to secure customer and internal data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introduce modern tools, frameworks, and processes to improve development speed and maintainability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with leadership to set technical direction, improve team workflows, and prioritize effectively in a fast-paced startup environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Desired Skills &amp; Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience: 5+ years of professional software development experience, with at least 2+ years in a senior or leadership capacity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backend/Infrastructure: Full proficiency in modern technologies (ex: Python, Go, Docker, K8S, Service Meshes, Terraform).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architecture Skills: Demonstrated ability to design and implement scalable systems and APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leadership: Proven ability to mentor and coach engineering teams in collaborative, early-stage environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quality-Driven: Strong focus on testing, maintainability, performance optimization, and security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup Mindset: Thrives in dynamic, evolving environments with shifting priorities and tight timelines.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base Salary: $150,000 - $190,000, depending on experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive equity package</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited paid time off</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (2 days per week in office)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Two company-wide offsites each year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>SimpleClosure is an equal opportunity employer</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.<br /></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"COMPANY OVERVIEW\n\nMost companies don't end in acquisition — they end in closure. Yet shutdown has never been given the same rigor, clarity, or professionalism as the moments that came before it. Nearly 4 million companies shut down every year, creating a massive, overlooked market. SimpleClosure is building the infrastructure to change that.\n\nHaving raised over $20M from leading VCs and trusted by more than 7,000 companies to date, we streamline the entire business dissolution process — from legal and tax to operational and administrative — as one coordinated effort instead of a patchwork of disconnected steps. We take it a step further by connecting founders with buyers for their remaining assets, so they can realize value that would otherwise be lost.\n\nJoining SimpleClosure means helping define an entirely new category, solving complex, high-impact problems, and building the products and processes that support founders through one of the most important moments in a company's journey.\n\n\n\n\nJOB OVERVIEW\n\nSimpleClosure is seeking an experienced Infrastructure Engineer to join Asset Hub, SimpleClosure's marketplace for the assets left behind when a company shuts down, including codebases, workspaces, proprietary data, and talent. Our buyers include some of the top foundation model labs, RL environment providers, and AI agent builders in the world, who rely on Asset Hub as a differentiated source of proprietary data and talent they can't get anywhere else. In this role, you’ll take the lead in building novel systems from the ground up that support digital asset acquisition, preparation and delivery. You’ll work closely with leadership, product, and design to ensure we deliver high-quality, scalable, and maintainable solutions. This position is hybrid in NYC and reports directly to the CTO.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Lead the technical design, development, and delivery of complex features from concept to deployment.\n\n - Mentor and guide other engineers, promoting strong engineering practices and continuous learning.\n\n - Architect scalable, maintainable systems across the stack, ensuring alignment with business goals.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally to translate product requirements into technical solutions.\n\n - Conduct and lead code reviews to maintain quality, performance, and security standards.\n\n - Build and configure the protective systems, processes, software, and networks to secure customer and internal data.\n\n - Introduce modern tools, frameworks, and processes to improve development speed and maintainability.\n\n - Partner with leadership to set technical direction, improve team workflows, and prioritize effectively in a fast-paced startup environment.\n\n\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Experience: 5+ years of professional software development experience, with at least 2+ years in a senior or leadership capacity.\n\n - Backend/Infrastructure: Full proficiency in modern technologies (ex: Python, Go, Docker, K8S, Service Meshes, Terraform).\n\n - Architecture Skills: Demonstrated ability to design and implement scalable systems and APIs.\n\n - Leadership: Proven ability to mentor and coach engineering teams in collaborative, early-stage environments.\n\n - Quality-Driven: Strong focus on testing, maintainability, performance optimization, and security.\n\n - Startup Mindset: Thrives in dynamic, evolving environments with shifting priorities and tight timelines.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Base Salary: $150,000 - $190,000, depending on experience level\n\n - Competitive equity package\n\n - Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, and vision\n\n - Life insurance\n\n - Unlimited paid time off\n\n - Flexible hybrid work environment in New York City, Midtown (2 days per week in office)\n\n - Two company-wide offsites each year\n\n - 401(k) with Traditional and Roth options, with immediate eligibility\n\n\n\n\nSIMPLECLOSURE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER\n\nWe are committed to providing a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at SimpleClosure — including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, and termination — are based on qualifications, merit, and business need, without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. We're committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please let us know.\n\n\n\nAPPLICATION PROCESS\n\nThanks for applying! If your experience is a strong match for what we're looking for, our hiring team will reach out to schedule an initial screening call and walk you through the rest of our interview process.\n\nWe do our best to respond to every applicant, but given the volume of applications we receive, we may not be able to provide individual updates if we decide not to move forward.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}